p0::
  name: "Ternary Microcontroller Chip"
  desc: """
    I have built a ternary concept microcontroller.
    The design has been tested and validated. I am
    a student. Help me get the chip fabricated by
    backing this project.
  """
  funding_range: 30000, 40000
  campaign_url: "https://github.com/phung-shook/my-chip"
  campaign_video: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=project-campaign-video-id"
  tags: "immediate", "nascent"
  license: "MIT"
  members::
    - ::
      uid: "uid0"
      fund_usage: """
        I will use the funds to buy a slot in a multi-chip-wafer
        shuttle from tiny tapeout. I'll get 10 chips this way. Can test, and
        even share some with the community.
      """

p1::
  name: "Semiconductor Fabrication for the learner in You"
  desc: """
    We are students setting up a simple semiconductor fabrication facility, at XYZ
    University. Initially, we aim to use proven designs based on work done by
    HackerFab IITB, which in turn builds on work done by HackerFab MIT.

    We plan to start by building the lowest cost lithographic machine,
    which still cost us one lakh rupees. We have pooled some money ourselves, to
    the tune of fourty thousand rupees. Please help us raise the remaining funds.

    We have plans to make this facility available to a larger collaborator group
    beyond our university. The funds you provide will likely create benefits over
    a larger area, beyond just Chennai - which happens to be where we are located.
  """
  funding_range: 80000, 100000
  campaign_url: "https://github.com/xyz-project/my-chip"
  campaign_video: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=project-campaign-video-id"
  tags: "short-term", "nascent"
  license: "MIT"
  members::
    - ::
      uid: "uid1"
      funding_range: 80000, 100000
      fund_usage: """
        I will be buying all the required equipments.
      """
    - ::
      # This user lends extra credibility to the project helps build trust and
      # accountability. Also benefits from the visibility
      uid: "uid2"
      funding_range: 0
      fund_usage: """
        Will be helping assemble, test and make the machine reusable.
      """
    - ::
      uid: "uid3"
      funding_range: 0
      fund_usage: """
        Will be helping tune the software. Will also document the work, so that any
        other university can reuse our work.
      """

p2::
  name: "For Schools, With Love: by the kids, for the kids"
  desc: """
    Join us students from the State of Kerala, as we say thanks to the creators of
    FunPlay - an incredible piece of software that we use everyday at school.

    Many of us had a discussion with the maintainer of the project about enhancements
    required for our school. It turned out we could ourselves do the required changes.
    The maintainer has kindly consented to guide us students in this, with assistance
    from some of our teachers. We are looking forward to the day when our school could
    potentially be running the software that we wrote, in atleast some small way! Our
    teachers tell us that there is no reason for other schools not to find this useful,
    but we are telling ourselves - one step at a time.

    The changes would require not only volunteer bandwidth, but also support logistics
    - travel, stay and multimedia recordings in studios for best quality. We already
    have a project plan drafted for this, accessible on our project page. This is a
    multi-phase project. We are seeking funds for Phase I right now.

    We are running this funding campaign to spread the awareness of the benefits of
    Free and Open Source Software by giving back in many different ways.

    Join us to say Thank you! Not limited to "Gods Own Country"... Gods from other
    countries are welcome too :) Help us expand the reach of FOSS in schools beyond Kerala.
  """
  funding_range: 100000, 150000
  campaign_url: "https://github.com/kerala-student-foss-project/with-love-for-schools"
  campaign_video: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=project-campaign-video-id"
  tags: "short-term", "nascent"
  license: "MIT"
  matching_grant::
    - ::
      uid: "mgid1"
  members::
    - ::
      uid: "uid4" # Student
    - ::
      uid: "uid5" # Student
    - ::
      uid: "uid6" # Guide
      fund_usage: """
        Training, Travel, Stay, High Quality recordings as detailed in Phase I
        document.
      """

p3::
  name: "To IndiaFOSS, With Love"
  desc: """
    We are five engineering students from IIT Guwahati, Assam. We are active contributors
    to various FOSS projects. We help organize local meetups, and help various people
    adopt FOSS.

    We also volunteer and run learning activities in a local(10+2) school, using Free and
    Open Source technologies. That said, we are painfully aware of the lack of awareness
    and opportunities available to these kids. One fine day, over our usual philosophical
    discussions, we asked ourselves, \"What if these folks got an opportunity to experience
    IndiaFOSS?\".

    IndiaFOSS is a vibrant technical festival, a geek's dream. But more importantly, it's
    a place where everyone is exposed to the entire spectrum of technologies - spanning
    not just software, but also hardware at various levels.

    It was 5 AM in the morning when we finished our philosophy detour. We were at the school
    at 9 AM. By 10 AM the school teacher was excited. And then we got cracking.

    Right now, we have a group of 24 students willing to travel all the way from Assam
    to Bengaluru. School teachers on the ready. And us too - to show them their paces
    in the conference and guide them at every step of the way.

    Help fund this dream of ours, and see you at IndiaFOSS. We'll keep you informed
    and entertained, and that's a promise! And the students and teachers will be back
    with a bang, bursting with new ideas, and ... a lot could happen over the next year
    with your support as the starting point.

    PS: we are requesting funding for roughly 80% of the cost, courtesy support of some
    good samaritans from Bengaluru. Your funding will cover the ticket cost(3AC) and
    some of the travel logistics for the entire group, excluding us students.
  """
  funding_range: 120000
  campaign_url: "https://ketto.org/to-indiafoss-with-love"
  campaign_video: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=project-campaign-video-id"
  tags: "short-term", "nascent"
  license: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  matching_grant::
    - ::
      uid: "mgid1"
  members::
    - ::
      uid: "uid4" # Student
    - ::
      uid: "uid5" # Student
    - ::
      uid: "uid6" # Guide
      fund_usage: """
        Training, Travel, Stay, High Quality recordings as detailed in Phase I
        document.
      """

# An example of a pure commons project
p4::
  name: "Heritage digitization for old palm-leaf collections, and pre British-era documents"
  desc: """
    My mother expired recently, and her last wish was that many of the historical artifacts
    that we possess be well preserved, and be made available to everyone.  We've had
    discussions with preservationists, and found a home for these rare and precious
    artefacts in a museum/archive.

    Meanwhile, another friend of ours came up with the brilliant idea that we could get
    these digitized in very high quality, and make them available to the entire world
    using online portals, free for any kind of use, forever. That appealed to us, and
    we felt that this was the best way to honour the wishes of our late mother.

    We dug deeper, and found out that this isn't exactly a simple thing. A home scanner,
    or a scanner that you would find in offices, is cheap and fast.  But it's not high
    quality - in the \"heritage\" sense.  Heritage scanners are expensive and primarily
    deployed in museums and some libraries. We were able to find some services that offer
    careful handling and high quality digitization of these artifacts, but they charge
    a significant price per page. And we have more than fifty thousand pages to scan!

    We are able to cover the cost of transportation and some more logistics, and around
    30% of the digitization, but for the rest we are looking for some support from you.
    With your support, we can get the digitization done and upload the entire scanned
    copies under a public access license. Post that, the documents will be shifted to
    the archive for permanent storage, and access by researchers.
  """
  funding_range: 200000
  campaign_url: "https://campaign.page/"
  campaign_video: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=project-campaign-video-id"
  tags: "short-term", "nascent"
  license: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  members::
    - ::
      uid: "uid7"
      fund_usage: """
        Heritage grade digitization of the royal family's private collection.
      """
